# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Pendahuluan {#introduction}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Physicist David DiVincenzo outlined five key requirements for any physical "
"implementation of a quantum computer, plus two additional criteria for "
"quantum communication. In this notebook, we will **experience each "
"DiVincenzo criterion through practical Qiskit demonstrations**. Rather than "
"going deep into theory, each section briefly explains one criterion and then"
" provides code exercises using Qiskit 2. You will get to run circuits on "
"simulators and real IBM Quantum devices to **explore each principle hands-"
"on**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fisikawan David DiVincenzo merumuskan lima persyaratan utama untuk setiap "
"implementasi fisik komputer kuantum, ditambah dua kriteria tambahan untuk "
"komunikasi kuantum. Dalam notebook ini, kita akan **mengalami setiap "
"kriteria DiVincenzo melalui demonstrasi Qiskit yang praktis**. Daripada "
"mendalami teori, setiap bagian menjelaskan satu kriteria secara singkat lalu"
" menyediakan latihan kode menggunakan Qiskit 2. Kamu akan menjalankan "
"Circuit pada simulator dan perangkat IBM Quantum nyata untuk "
"**mengeksplorasi setiap prinsip secara langsung**.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**DiVincenzo’s Five Criteria for Quantum Computation**:\n"
msgstr "**Lima Kriteria DiVincenzo untuk Komputasi Kuantum**:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**A scalable physical system with well-characterized qubits.**\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sistem fisik yang skalabel dengan qubit yang terkarakterisasi dengan "
"baik.**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Ability to initialize qubits** to a simple fiducial state (e.g. |00…0〉).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kemampuan menginisialisasi qubit** ke keadaan fiducial sederhana (mis. "
"|00…0〉).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Long decoherence times** (qubit coherence much longer than gate operation "
"time).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Waktu dekoherensi yang panjang** (koherensi qubit jauh lebih panjang dari "
"waktu operasi Gate).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A universal set of quantum gates** (able to perform arbitrary unitary "
"operations).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Seperangkat Gate kuantum universal** (mampu melakukan operasi uniter "
"sembarang).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Qubit-specific measurement capability** (read out the state of each "
"qubit).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kemampuan pengukuran spesifik per qubit** (membaca keadaan setiap "
"qubit).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*(DiVincenzo also described two criteria for quantum communication: the "
"ability to interconvert stationary and “flying” qubits, and to faithfully "
"transmit flying qubits between locations. We include these in a recommended "
"activity at the end of this notebook.)*\n"
msgstr ""
"*(DiVincenzo juga mendeskripsikan dua kriteria untuk komunikasi kuantum: "
"kemampuan untuk saling mengonversi qubit stasioner dan qubit \"terbang\", "
"serta mengirimkan qubit terbang secara akurat antar lokasi. Kita memasukkan "
"ini dalam aktivitas yang direkomendasikan di akhir notebook ini.)*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each of the following sections corresponds to one criterion. We'll use "
"Qiskit to illustrate the concept with code and **interactive experiments** "
"you can try. For example, we will see how scaling up the number of qubits "
"and circuit depth affects outcomes (Criterion 1), how to reset and prepare "
"qubit states (Criterion 2), how to measure qubits on simulators vs real "
"devices (Criterion 4), how Qiskit composes universal gates (Criterion 3), "
"and how finite coherence (T₁, T₂) impacts computations (Criterion 5). By the"
" end, you'll have a deeper intuition for what each DiVincenzo criterion "
"means in practice and how Qiskit enables experimenting with them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap bagian berikut berkaitan dengan satu kriteria. Kita akan menggunakan "
"Qiskit untuk mengilustrasikan konsep dengan kode dan **eksperimen "
"interaktif** yang bisa kamu coba. Misalnya, kita akan melihat bagaimana "
"menambah jumlah qubit dan kedalaman Circuit memengaruhi hasil (Kriteria 1), "
"cara mereset dan menyiapkan keadaan qubit (Kriteria 2), cara mengukur qubit "
"pada simulator vs perangkat nyata (Kriteria 4), bagaimana Qiskit menyusun "
"Gate universal (Kriteria 3), dan bagaimana koherensi terbatas (T₁, T₂) "
"memengaruhi komputasi (Kriteria 5). Di akhir, kamu akan memiliki intuisi "
"yang lebih dalam tentang apa arti setiap kriteria DiVincenzo dalam praktik "
"dan bagaimana Qiskit memungkinkan kita bereksperimen dengannya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. Criterion 1 – Scalable, Well-Characterized Qubits "
"{#1-criterion-1-scalable-well-characterized-qubits}"
msgstr ""
"1. Kriteria 1 – qubit yang Skalabel dan Terkarakterisasi dengan Baik "
"{#1-criterion-1-scalable-well-characterized-qubits}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Criterion 1:** *“A scalable physical system with well characterized "
"qubits.”* This means we need a quantum hardware platform where we can "
"**increase the number of qubits** and still control them reliably. Each "
"qubit’s properties (energy levels, error rates, connectivity, etc.) should "
"be well understood. Essentially, we want to build bigger circuits without "
"the system breaking down. In practice, as we scale up qubit count or circuit"
" depth, errors and decoherence accumulate, so demonstrating *scalability* "
"also means understanding how increasing size affects performance.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kriteria 1:** *\"Sistem fisik yang skalabel dengan qubit yang "
"terkarakterisasi dengan baik.\"* Ini berarti kita membutuhkan platform "
"perangkat keras kuantum di mana kita bisa **meningkatkan jumlah qubit** dan "
"tetap mengendalikannya secara andal. Sifat-sifat setiap qubit (tingkat "
"energi, tingkat kesalahan, konektivitas, dll.) harus dipahami dengan baik. "
"Intinya, kita ingin membangun Circuit yang lebih besar tanpa sistem runtuh. "
"Dalam praktik, saat kita menambah jumlah qubit atau kedalaman Circuit, "
"kesalahan dan dekoherensi terakumulasi, sehingga menunjukkan *skalabilitas* "
"juga berarti memahami bagaimana peningkatan ukuran memengaruhi performa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Goal of Demo:** Use Qiskit to show the effect of scaling up a circuit (in "
"qubit count or gate depth) on the output fidelity. We’ll simulate an ideal "
"vs noisy scenario to see how a larger system or deeper circuit succumbs to "
"decoherence and errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tujuan Demo:** Gunakan Qiskit untuk menunjukkan efek penskalaan Circuit "
"(dalam jumlah qubit atau kedalaman Gate) terhadap fidelitas output. Kita "
"akan mensimulasikan skenario ideal vs berisik untuk melihat bagaimana sistem"
" yang lebih besar atau Circuit yang lebih dalam rentan terhadap dekoherensi "
"dan kesalahan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's construct a small entangled state (GHZ state) on 3 qubits, then"
" a larger one on 5 qubits, as a simple scaling test. A GHZ state of *n* "
"qubits is $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0...0\\rangle + |1...1\\rangle)$. In an "
"ideal simulation, measuring an n-qubit GHZ yields only two outcomes (all 0s "
"or all 1s) with equal probability. We will compare the **ideal output** to a"
" **noisy output** as we increase n or circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, mari buat keadaan terjalin kecil (keadaan GHZ) pada 3 qubit, "
"kemudian yang lebih besar pada 5 qubit, sebagai uji skalabilitas sederhana. "
"Keadaan GHZ dari *n* qubit adalah $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0...0\\rangle + "
"|1...1\\rangle)$. Dalam simulasi ideal, mengukur GHZ n-Qubit hanya "
"menghasilkan dua keluaran (semua 0 atau semua 1) dengan probabilitas yang "
"sama. Kita akan membandingkan **output ideal** dengan **output berisik** "
"saat kita meningkatkan n atau kedalaman Circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Expected outcome (ideal case):** The 3-qubit GHZ ideally yields roughly "
"50% `000` and 50% `111` in the counts. The 5-qubit GHZ yields ~50% `00000` "
"and 50% `11111`. No other bit-strings appear because the state is ideally "
"fully coherent and entangled. You should see two tall bars on the histogram "
"for each circuit corresponding to all-zeros and all-ones outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hasil yang diharapkan (kasus ideal):** GHZ 3 qubit secara ideal "
"menghasilkan sekitar 50% `000` dan 50% `111` dalam hitungan. GHZ 5 qubit "
"menghasilkan ~50% `00000` dan 50% `11111`. Tidak ada bitstring lain yang "
"muncul karena keadaan ini secara ideal sepenuhnya koheren dan terjalin. Kamu"
" seharusnya melihat dua bar tinggi pada histogram untuk setiap sirkuit yang "
"sesuai dengan keluaran semua-nol dan semua-satu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, let's see what happens in a **noisy environment**. We will use Qiskit "
"Aer’s noise model capabilities to mimic a real device’s errors. For example,"
" we can take an IBM backend’s properties to create a noise model that "
"includes gate errors, finite gate times, qubit relaxation (T₁), dephasing "
"(T₂), and readout errors. Here, we’ll use a **fake backend** that represents"
" the IBM Quantum Brisbane device to generate a noise model, and re-run the "
"GHZ circuits through that.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, mari lihat apa yang terjadi di **lingkungan berisik**. Kita "
"akan menggunakan kemampuan model noise Qiskit Aer untuk meniru kesalahan "
"perangkat nyata. Misalnya, kita bisa mengambil properti backend IBM untuk "
"membuat model noise yang mencakup kesalahan Gate, waktu Gate terbatas, "
"relaksasi qubit (T₁), dephasing (T₂), dan kesalahan readout. Di sini, kita "
"akan menggunakan **fake backend** yang merepresentasikan perangkat IBM "
"Quantum Brisbane untuk menghasilkan model noise, dan menjalankan kembali "
"Circuit GHZ melaluinya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise 1a: Simulate with Noise {#exercise-1a-simulate-with-noise}"
msgstr "Latihan 1a: Simulasi dengan Noise {#exercise-1a-simulate-with-noise}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Complete the code below to simulate the GHZ circuits on a noisy simulator "
"based on the `FakeBrisbane` backend. This will show you how performance "
"degrades as the system scales in a realistic noise environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lengkapi kode di bawah ini untuk mensimulasikan Circuit GHZ pada simulator "
"berisik berdasarkan backend `FakeBrisbane`. Ini akan menunjukkan bagaimana "
"performa menurun saat sistem diskalakan dalam lingkungan noise yang "
"realistis.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exercise 1b: Run on real IBM Quantum computer {#exercise-1b-run-on-real-ibm-"
"quantum-computer}"
msgstr ""
"Latihan 1b: Jalankan di komputer IBM Quantum nyata {#exercise-1b-run-on-"
"real-ibm-quantum-computer}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code below runs the GHZ circuits on a real IBM Quantum computer. This "
"will show you how performance degrades on a real device.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kode di bawah ini menjalankan Circuit GHZ pada komputer IBM Quantum nyata. "
"Ini akan menunjukkan bagaimana performa menurun pada perangkat nyata.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Expected outcome (noisy vs ideal):** With noise, whether simulated or on a"
" real device, the GHZ state is **less perfect**. You will see additional "
"outcomes beyond all-0s and all-1s. For 3 qubits, instead of 100% in "
"`000`/`111`, some probability leaks into other bitstrings (e.g. `001`, "
"`010`, etc.) due to gate errors or decoherence flipping some qubits. For 5 "
"qubits, the effect is even more pronounced; the larger circuit (more qubits "
"and CNOT gates) accumulates more error, so the all-0 and all-1 peaks are "
"lower, and many other outcomes appear. This trend illustrates the challenge "
"of *scalability*: as we scale up, maintaining high fidelity gets harder "
"without error correction.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hasil yang diharapkan (berisik vs ideal):** Dengan noise, baik yang "
"disimulasikan maupun di perangkat nyata, keadaan GHZ **kurang sempurna**. "
"Kamu akan melihat keluaran tambahan di luar semua-0 dan semua-1. Untuk 3 "
"qubit, alih-alih 100% di `000`/`111`, sebagian probabilitas bocor ke "
"bitstring lain (mis. `001`, `010`, dll.) karena kesalahan Gate atau "
"dekoherensi yang membalik beberapa qubit. Untuk 5 qubit, efeknya bahkan "
"lebih terasa; Circuit yang lebih besar (lebih banyak qubit dan Gate CNOT) "
"mengakumulasi lebih banyak kesalahan, sehingga puncak semua-0 dan semua-1 "
"lebih rendah, dan banyak keluaran lain muncul. Tren ini menggambarkan "
"tantangan *skalabilitas*: saat kita menambah skala, mempertahankan fidelitas"
" tinggi semakin sulit tanpa koreksi kesalahan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Insight:** A scalable quantum computer needs to preserve quantum "
"correlations as the system grows. Our examples show how increasing qubit "
"count/gate depth causes outcome fidelity to drop when noise is present. The "
"remaining criteria will deal with keeping those qubits well-behaved (low "
"error, initializable, etc.) as we scale.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Wawasan:** Komputer kuantum yang skalabel perlu mempertahankan korelasi "
"kuantum saat sistem berkembang. Contoh-contoh kita menunjukkan bagaimana "
"meningkatkan jumlah qubit/kedalaman Gate menyebabkan fidelitas keluaran "
"menurun saat noise hadir. Kriteria-kriteria lainnya akan membahas cara "
"menjaga qubit-Qubit tersebut berperilaku baik (kesalahan rendah, dapat "
"diinisialisasi, dll.) saat kita menambah skala.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. Criterion 2 – Qubit Initialization {#2-criterion-2-qubit-initialization}"
msgstr ""
"2. Kriteria 2 – Inisialisasi qubit {#2-criterion-2-qubit-initialization}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Criterion 2:** *“The ability to initialize the state of the qubits to a "
"simple fiducial state, such as |000…〉.”* All qubits should reliably start in"
" a known reference state (typically the ground state |0〉 for each qubit). "
"Initialization is essential so that algorithms begin on a clean slate. In "
"practice, on IBM quantum devices each qubit is automatically reset to |0〉 at"
" the start of each circuit execution. Qiskit also provides instructions to "
"reset qubits or prepare custom states during a computation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kriteria 2:** *\"Kemampuan untuk menginisialisasi keadaan qubit ke keadaan"
" fiducial sederhana, seperti |000…〉.\"* Semua qubit harus selalu dimulai "
"dalam keadaan referensi yang diketahui (biasanya keadaan dasar |0〉 untuk "
"setiap qubit). Inisialisasi sangat penting agar algoritma dimulai dari awal "
"yang bersih. Dalam praktik, pada perangkat kuantum IBM, setiap qubit secara "
"otomatis direset ke |0〉 di awal setiap eksekusi Circuit. Qiskit juga "
"menyediakan instruksi untuk mereset qubit atau menyiapkan keadaan kustom "
"selama komputasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Goal of Demo:** Show how to initialize qubits in Qiskit, both at the start"
" and mid-circuit. We will demonstrate using the `reset` instruction and "
"state preparation methods.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tujuan Demo:** Tunjukkan cara menginisialisasi qubit di Qiskit, baik di "
"awal maupun di tengah Circuit. Kita akan mendemonstrasikan penggunaan "
"instruksi `reset` dan metode persiapan keadaan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exercise 2: Prepare a Specific State {#exercise-2-prepare-a-specific-state}"
msgstr ""
"Latihan 2: Siapkan Keadaan Tertentu {#exercise-2-prepare-a-specific-state}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the code block below, complete the `QuantumCircuit` to prepare the state "
"$|10\\rangle$. This means qubit 0 should be in state $|0\\rangle$ and qubit "
"1 should be in state $|1\\rangle$. Use the appropriate gate and instruction "
"to achieve this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam blok kode di bawah ini, lengkapi `QuantumCircuit` untuk menyiapkan "
"keadaan $|10\\rangle$. Ini berarti qubit 0 harus berada dalam keadaan "
"$|0\\rangle$ dan qubit 1 harus berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$. Gunakan "
"Gate dan instruksi yang tepat untuk mencapai ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should see `10` (binary for qubit1=1, qubit0=0) with 100% probability "
"from the simulation, meaning qubit 1 was successfully prepared in |1〉 and "
"qubit 0 in |0〉.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu seharusnya melihat `10` (biner untuk qubit1=1, qubit0=0) dengan "
"probabilitas 100% dari simulasi, yang berarti qubit 1 berhasil disiapkan "
"dalam |1〉 dan qubit 0 dalam |0〉.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, for a more general state preparation, Qiskit allows initialization to "
"arbitrary states using the `initialize` method. For example, let's prepare a"
" qubit in the state $|+\\rangle = (|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$, which "
"is a superposition state, and a pair of qubits in the Bell state "
"$(|00\\rangle+|11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, untuk persiapan keadaan yang lebih umum, Qiskit memungkinkan "
"inisialisasi ke keadaan sembarang menggunakan metode `initialize`. Misalnya,"
" mari siapkan sebuah qubit dalam keadaan $|+\\rangle = "
"(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$, yang merupakan keadaan superposisi, dan "
"sepasang qubit dalam keadaan Bell $(|00\\rangle+|11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Expected outcomes:** The single qubit |+〉 state, when measured, will yield"
" `0` and `1` with roughly 50% probability each. The Bell state measurement "
"should give roughly 50% `00` and 50% `11`. If you see these, it confirms our"
" initialization to those states was successful.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hasil yang diharapkan:** Keadaan |+〉 satu qubit, saat diukur, akan "
"menghasilkan `0` dan `1` dengan probabilitas sekitar 50% masing-masing. "
"Pengukuran keadaan Bell seharusnya menghasilkan sekitar 50% `00` dan 50% "
"`11`. Jika kamu melihat ini, itu mengonfirmasi inisialisasi kita ke keadaan-"
"keadaan tersebut berhasil.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Mid-circuit initialization:** Qiskit’s `reset` can be used in the middle "
"of a circuit to reinitialize a qubit to |0〉 on the fly. For instance, in "
"error correction codes or iterative algorithms, one often measures a qubit "
"and then resets it for reuse. The `reset` operation is deterministic; it "
"dumps any existing state and cools the qubit down to ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Inisialisasi di tengah Circuit:** `reset` Qiskit dapat digunakan di tengah"
" Circuit untuk menginisialisasi ulang sebuah qubit ke |0〉 saat sedang "
"berjalan. Misalnya, dalam kode koreksi kesalahan atau algoritma iteratif, "
"seseorang sering mengukur qubit lalu meresetnnya untuk digunakan kembali. "
"Operasi `reset` bersifat deterministik; ia membuang keadaan yang ada dan "
"mendinginkan qubit ke keadaan dasar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Device example:** On hardware like **ibmq_brisbane** (127 qubits) or any "
"IBM device, all qubits start in |0〉 by default when a job is run. If you "
"needed a different starting state, you’d apply gates at the beginning (as we"
" did with X to get |1〉). Continuous re-initialization (for quantum error "
"correction) is an active research topic because doing it quickly is "
"challenging. Thankfully, for basic use, the ability to start fresh in |0…0〉 "
"is available and we demonstrated how to achieve other desired starting "
"states too.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Contoh perangkat:** Pada perangkat keras seperti **ibmq_brisbane** (127 "
"qubit) atau perangkat IBM apa pun, semua qubit dimulai dalam |0〉 secara "
"default saat sebuah job dijalankan. Jika kamu membutuhkan keadaan awal yang "
"berbeda, kamu perlu menerapkan Gate di awal (seperti yang kita lakukan "
"dengan X untuk mendapatkan |1〉). Inisialisasi ulang yang berkelanjutan "
"(untuk koreksi kesalahan kuantum) adalah topik penelitian aktif karena "
"melakukannya dengan cepat merupakan tantangan tersendiri. Untungnya, untuk "
"penggunaan dasar, kemampuan untuk memulai dari awal di |0…0〉 tersedia dan "
"kita telah mendemonstrasikan cara mencapai keadaan awal yang diinginkan "
"lainnya juga.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3. Criterion 3 – Long Coherence Time (Decoherence vs Gate Time) "
"{#3-criterion-3-long-coherence-time-decoherence-vs-gate-time}"
msgstr ""
"3. Kriteria 3 – Waktu Koherensi yang Panjang (Dekoherensi vs Waktu Gate) "
"{#3-criterion-3-long-coherence-time-decoherence-vs-gate-time}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Criterion 3:** *“Long relevant decoherence times, much longer than the "
"gate operation time.”* This addresses the need for qubits to maintain their "
"quantum state long enough to perform the necessary operations. Each qubit "
"has a **T₁ time** (energy relaxation time, how quickly |1〉 decays to |0〉) "
"and **T₂ time** (dephasing time, how quickly relative phase coherence is "
"lost). For a quantum computer to work, these timescales should greatly "
"exceed the duration of gate operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kriteria 3:** *\"Waktu dekoherensi yang relevan harus jauh lebih panjang "
"dari waktu operasi gate.\"* Ini menegaskan kebutuhan qubit untuk "
"mempertahankan keadaan kuantumnya cukup lama agar semua operasi yang "
"diperlukan dapat dilakukan. Setiap qubit memiliki **waktu T₁** (waktu "
"relaksasi energi, seberapa cepat |1〉 meluruh ke |0〉) dan **waktu T₂** (waktu"
" dephasing, seberapa cepat koherensi fase relatif hilang). Agar komputer "
"kuantum bisa bekerja, skala waktu ini harus jauh melebihi durasi operasi "
"gate.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Goal of Demo:** Investigate qubit coherence in Qiskit by showing how "
"decoherence impacts circuit outcomes as execution length grows. We’ll use a "
"fake backend with known T1/T2 times to simulate this effect.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tujuan Demo:** Menyelidiki koherensi qubit di Qiskit dengan memperlihatkan"
" bagaimana dekoherensi memengaruhi hasil Circuit seiring bertambahnya "
"panjang eksekusi. Kita akan menggunakan fake backend dengan waktu T1/T2 yang"
" sudah diketahui untuk mensimulasikan efek ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To **demonstrate the impact of finite coherence**, we'll simulate a T1 decay"
" experiment. We will prepare a qubit in the |1〉 state, wait for some time "
"using a `delay` instruction, and then measure. We expect the probability of "
"measuring |1〉 to decrease as the delay increases.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk **mendemonstrasikan dampak koherensi terbatas**, kita akan "
"mensimulasikan eksperimen peluruhan T1. Kita akan menyiapkan qubit dalam "
"keadaan |1〉, menunggu beberapa saat menggunakan instruksi `delay`, lalu "
"mengukurnya. Kita mengharapkan probabilitas mengukur |1〉 menurun seiring "
"bertambahnya delay.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exercise 3: Simulate a T1 Decay Experiment {#exercise-3-simulate-a-t1-decay-"
"experiment}"
msgstr ""
"Latihan 3: Simulasi Eksperimen Peluruhan T1 {#exercise-3-simulate-"
"a-t1-decay-experiment}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, use a noisy simulator based on `FakeVigo` (which has T1 times of "
"~50-100 µs) to run these circuits. The simulator will automatically apply "
"the T1/T2 errors during the `delay` instructions. Transpile the circuits for"
" this backend and execute them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, gunakan simulator bising berdasarkan `FakeVigo` (yang memiliki "
"waktu T1 sekitar 50-100 µs) untuk menjalankan circuit-circuit ini. Simulator"
" akan secara otomatis menerapkan error T1/T2 selama instruksi `delay`. "
"Transpile circuit-circuit tersebut untuk backend ini dan eksekusi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"4. Criterion 4 – Universal Set of Quantum Gates {#4-criterion-4-universal-"
"set-of-quantum-gates}"
msgstr ""
"4. Kriteria 4 – Set Gate Kuantum Universal {#4-criterion-4-universal-set-of-"
"quantum-gates}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Criterion 4:** *“A ‘universal’ set of quantum gates.”* This means our "
"hardware must allow us to perform *any* quantum computation by composing a "
"finite set of basic gates. In classical computing, NAND is universal; in "
"quantum, there are many choices of universal gate sets (e.g. \\{H, T, "
"CNOT\\} or the native gates of a given machine). The IBM devices, for "
"example, have a set of native operations like arbitrary single-qubit "
"rotations and CNOTs between certain qubits, which together are universal. "
"Qiskit’s job is often to **compile high-level gates into these basis "
"gates**.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kriteria 4:** *\"Sebuah set gate kuantum yang 'universal'.\"* Ini berarti "
"hardware kita harus memungkinkan kita melakukan *komputasi kuantum apa pun* "
"dengan menyusun sekumpulan gate dasar yang terbatas. Dalam komputasi klasik,"
" NAND bersifat universal; dalam komputasi kuantum, ada banyak pilihan set "
"gate universal (misalnya \\{H, T, CNOT\\} atau gate native dari mesin "
"tertentu). Perangkat IBM, misalnya, memiliki sekumpulan operasi native "
"seperti rotasi single-qubit arbitrer dan CNOT antara qubit tertentu, yang "
"bersama-sama bersifat universal. Tugas Qiskit sering kali adalah "
"**mengkompilasi gate tingkat tinggi ke dalam gate basis tersebut**.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Goal of Demo:** Illustrate gate universality by showing how Qiskit "
"decomposes gates. We’ll take a non-native gate (like a 3-qubit Toffoli gate,"
" CCX) and see how it breaks down into the device’s basis gates. This "
"demonstrates that the provided gate set is indeed *universal* – it can "
"produce the more complex operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tujuan Demo:** Mengilustrasikan universalitas gate dengan memperlihatkan "
"cara Qiskit mendekomposisi gate. Kita akan mengambil gate non-native "
"(seperti Toffoli 3-Qubit, CCX) dan melihat cara gate itu dipecah menjadi "
"gate basis perangkat. Ini menunjukkan bahwa set gate yang disediakan memang "
"*universal* – set itu dapat menghasilkan operasi yang lebih kompleks.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let’s see what the basis gates are for a typical IBM backend. We’ll query the configuration of a device (or its fake version). For instance, ibmq_brisbane’s basis gates:\n"
"You should observe the probability `P(qubit=1)` decreasing as the delay time increases, following an exponential decay curve characteristic of T1 relaxation. This directly demonstrates how finite coherence time leads to computational errors if the circuit runs for too long.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, mari kita lihat apa saja gate basis untuk backend IBM yang khas. Kita akan mengquery konfigurasi sebuah perangkat (atau versi fake-nya). Misalnya, gate basis ibmq_brisbane:\n"
"Kamu seharusnya melihat probabilitas `P(qubit=1)` menurun seiring bertambahnya waktu delay, mengikuti kurva peluruhan eksponensial yang merupakan karakteristik relaksasi T1. Ini secara langsung menunjukkan bagaimana waktu koherensi terbatas menyebabkan error komputasi jika Circuit berjalan terlalu lama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Impact on algorithms:** If you try a longer algorithm (with many "
"sequential gates), the total execution time might approach or exceed T2, "
"causing the state to lose coherence before the end. This is why improving "
"coherence times and making gates faster are two of the most critical goals "
"in quantum hardware research.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Dampak pada algoritma:** Jika kamu mencoba algoritma yang lebih panjang "
"(dengan banyak gate berurutan), total waktu eksekusi mungkin mendekati atau "
"melebihi T2, menyebabkan keadaan kehilangan koherensi sebelum selesai. "
"Inilah mengapa meningkatkan waktu koherensi dan mempercepat gate adalah dua "
"tujuan paling kritis dalam riset hardware kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This might output something like `['id', 'rz', 'sx', 'x', 'ecr']`. These are"
" the primitive operations the hardware natively supports (Identity/no-op, RZ"
" rotation, sqrt(X) gate, X gate, and controlled-X). Any other gate must be "
"composed from these. This set is known to be universal for quantum computing"
" (essentially single-qubit rotations plus an entangling two-qubit gate form "
"a universal set).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini mungkin menghasilkan sesuatu seperti `['id', 'rz', 'sx', 'x', 'ecr']`. "
"Ini adalah operasi primitif yang didukung hardware secara native "
"(Identity/no-op, rotasi RZ, gate sqrt(X), gate X, dan controlled-X). Gate "
"lainnya harus disusun dari ini. Set ini diketahui bersifat universal untuk "
"komputasi kuantum (pada dasarnya rotasi single-qubit ditambah gate two-qubit"
" yang menghasilkan entanglement membentuk set universal).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, take a **Toffoli (CCX) gate** as a test case. CCX flips a target qubit "
"only if two control qubits are both 1. It’s not a native gate on IBM "
"hardware. Qiskit provides a `ccx` instruction, but under the hood it will "
"decompose it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, ambil **gate Toffoli (CCX)** sebagai kasus uji. CCX membalik qubit"
" target hanya jika dua qubit kontrol keduanya bernilai 1. Ini bukan gate "
"native di hardware IBM. Qiskit menyediakan instruksi `ccx`, tetapi di balik "
"itu akan mendekomposisinya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exercise 4: Decompose a Toffoli Gate {#exercise-4-decompose-a-toffoli-gate}"
msgstr ""
"Latihan 4: Dekomposisi Gate Toffoli {#exercise-4-decompose-a-toffoli-gate}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Complete the code below to build a circuit with a Toffoli (CCX) gate and "
"then use Qiskit to break it down into the native basis gates of the "
"`FakeBrisbane` backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lengkapi kode di bawah ini untuk membangun Circuit dengan gate Toffoli "
"(CCX), lalu gunakan Qiskit untuk memecahnya menjadi gate basis native dari "
"backend `FakeBrisbane`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the transpiled output, you should see the CCX replaced by a sequence of "
"more basic gates like `rz`, `sx`, and `ecr`. This proves that the native "
"gates are sufficient to express the Toffoli.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam output hasil transpile, kamu seharusnya melihat CCX digantikan oleh "
"serangkaian gate yang lebih dasar seperti `rz`, `sx`, dan `ecr`. Ini "
"membuktikan bahwa gate native sudah cukup untuk mengekspresikan Toffoli.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Universality in practice:** The exercise above shows that a complex "
"3-qubit gate was built from simpler ones. In general, **any** multi-qubit "
"unitary can be composed from 1- and 2-qubit gates. The transpiler is a "
"crucial component of any quantum software stack, as it bridges the gap "
"between the abstract algorithms we want to run and the physical operations a"
" specific quantum device can actually perform.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Universalitas dalam praktik:** Latihan di atas memperlihatkan bahwa gate "
"3-Qubit yang kompleks dibangun dari gate yang lebih sederhana. Secara umum, "
"**sembarang** unitary multi-Qubit dapat disusun dari gate 1- dan 2-Qubit. "
"Transpiler adalah komponen krusial dari stack software kuantum mana pun, "
"karena menjembatani kesenjangan antara algoritma abstrak yang ingin kita "
"jalankan dan operasi fisik yang benar-benar bisa dilakukan oleh perangkat "
"kuantum tertentu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Device example:** The **ibmq_brisbane**  device uses the Eagle "
"architecture with basis gates shown above. That means any algorithm sent to "
"those machines will be converted into sequences of those operations. This "
"criterion is essentially about **controllability**; we have enough control "
"knobs to do any needed operation on our qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Contoh perangkat:** Perangkat **ibmq_brisbane** menggunakan arsitektur "
"Eagle dengan gate basis seperti yang ditunjukkan di atas. Artinya, setiap "
"algoritma yang dikirim ke mesin-mesin tersebut akan dikonversi menjadi "
"urutan operasi tersebut. Kriteria ini pada dasarnya tentang **kemampuan "
"kontrol**; kita memiliki cukup knob kontrol untuk melakukan operasi apa pun "
"yang diperlukan pada qubit kita.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5. Criterion 5 – Qubit Measurement {#5-criterion-5-qubit-measurement}"
msgstr "5. Kriteria 5 – Pengukuran qubit {#5-criterion-5-qubit-measurement}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Criterion 5:** *“A qubit-specific measurement capability.”* Every qubit’s "
"state must be measurable (typically in the computational basis, |0〉 or |1〉)."
" In other words, after running a quantum circuit, we need to read out each "
"qubit as a 0/1 classical bit. This criterion is about having reliable "
"detectors for each qubit and being able to select which qubits to measure.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kriteria 5:** *\"Kemampuan pengukuran khusus per qubit.\"* Keadaan setiap "
"qubit harus bisa diukur (biasanya dalam basis komputasi, |0〉 atau |1〉). "
"Dengan kata lain, setelah menjalankan Circuit kuantum, kita perlu membaca "
"setiap qubit sebagai bit klasik 0/1. Kriteria ini tentang memiliki detektor "
"yang andal untuk setiap qubit dan kemampuan untuk memilih qubit mana yang "
"akan diukur.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Goal of Demo:** Show how to perform measurements in Qiskit on simulators "
"and real devices, and highlight the differences (like measurement noise). We"
" will measure some qubits in various states and examine the results. We’ll "
"also demonstrate how readout errors might appear by comparing simulator vs "
"hardware results.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tujuan Demo:** Memperlihatkan cara melakukan pengukuran di Qiskit pada "
"simulator dan perangkat nyata, serta menyoroti perbedaan-perbedaannya "
"(seperti noise pengukuran). Kita akan mengukur beberapa qubit dalam berbagai"
" keadaan dan memeriksa hasilnya. Kita juga akan menunjukkan bagaimana error "
"readout mungkin muncul dengan membandingkan hasil simulator vs hardware.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First, a simple measurement example:\n"
msgstr "Pertama, contoh pengukuran sederhana:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We expect 1000 counts of `01` on the simulator. Now, let’s see **measurement"
" error** in action by simulating it. We can add a readout error to our Aer "
"simulator. Qiskit Aer allows us to define a `ReadoutError` and attach it to "
"qubits in a noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mengharapkan 1000 hitungan `01` pada simulator. Sekarang, mari kita "
"lihat **error pengukuran** secara langsung dengan mensimulasikannya. Kita "
"bisa menambahkan error readout ke simulator Aer kita. Qiskit Aer "
"memungkinkan kita mendefinisikan `ReadoutError` dan melampirkannya ke qubit "
"dalam noise model.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exercise 5: Simulate Readout Error {#exercise-5-simulate-readout-error}"
msgstr ""
"Latihan 5: Simulasi Error Readout {#exercise-5-simulate-readout-error}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Complete the code to define a simple readout error model where each qubit "
"has a 2% chance of being measured incorrectly (a 0 is read as a 1, or a 1 as"
" a 0). Then, run the measurement circuit with this noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lengkapi kode untuk mendefinisikan model error readout sederhana di mana "
"setiap qubit memiliki peluang 2% diukur secara keliru (0 terbaca sebagai 1, "
"atau 1 terbaca sebagai 0). Kemudian, jalankan Circuit pengukuran dengan "
"noise model ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This simulated output will show some erroneous counts (like `11`, `00`, "
"`10`) similar to what real hardware might produce, demonstrating the impact "
"of imperfect measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Output simulasi ini akan menunjukkan beberapa hitungan yang salah (seperti "
"`11`, `00`, `10`) mirip dengan apa yang mungkin dihasilkan hardware nyata, "
"menunjukkan dampak pengukuran yang tidak sempurna.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Device example:** On a real device like **ibmq_brisbane**, you could run "
"the same circuit and would likely see similar, non-zero counts for the "
"incorrect outcomes. The device calibration data lists a readout error for "
"each qubit. Being able to target and read specific qubits is crucial, and "
"understanding their error characteristics is key to getting meaningful "
"results. Running on a real device was demonstrated in **Exercise 1b: Run on "
"real IBM Quantum computer**.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Contoh perangkat:** Pada perangkat nyata seperti **ibmq_brisbane**, kamu "
"bisa menjalankan Circuit yang sama dan kemungkinan akan melihat hitungan "
"non-nol yang serupa untuk hasil yang salah. Data kalibrasi perangkat "
"mencantumkan error readout untuk setiap qubit. Kemampuan untuk menarget dan "
"membaca qubit tertentu sangatlah penting, dan memahami karakteristik "
"errornya adalah kunci untuk mendapatkan hasil yang bermakna. Menjalankan "
"pada perangkat nyata sudah didemonstrasikan di **Latihan 1b: Jalankan di "
"komputer IBM Quantum nyata**.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum Communication Criteria (Flying Qubits) {#quantum-communication-"
"criteria-flying-qubits}"
msgstr ""
"Kriteria Komunikasi Kuantum (Flying qubit) {#quantum-communication-criteria-"
"flying-qubits}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"DiVincenzo also listed two criteria specific to quantum communication, "
"important if building a networked quantum computer:\n"
msgstr ""
"DiVincenzo juga mencantumkan dua kriteria khusus untuk komunikasi kuantum, "
"penting jika membangun komputer kuantum yang terjaringan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Ability to interconvert stationary and flying qubits.** (E.g., map a qubit"
" in a processor to a photon that can travel.)\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kemampuan untuk saling mengkonversi qubit stasioner dan flying qubit.** "
"(Misalnya, memetakan qubit di prosesor ke foton yang bisa bergerak.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Ability to faithfully transmit flying qubits between locations.** (E.g., "
"send a photon qubit through a fiber without losing quantum information.)\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kemampuan untuk mentransmisikan flying qubit secara akurat antar lokasi.**"
" (Misalnya, mengirim qubit foton melalui serat optik tanpa kehilangan "
"informasi kuantum.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These are beyond standard Qiskit usage because Qiskit primarily deals with "
"stationary qubits on a chip. However, we can illustrate the *concept* of "
"these criteria with a simple example: **quantum teleportation**. "
"Teleportation shows converting a stationary qubit’s state into information "
"carried by an entangled pair (the \"flying\" part) and classical "
"communication, which is then used to reconstruct the state on another "
"stationary qubit elsewhere.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini di luar penggunaan Qiskit standar karena Qiskit terutama menangani qubit"
" stasioner di chip. Namun, kita bisa mengilustrasikan *konsep* kriteria ini "
"dengan contoh sederhana: **teleportasi kuantum**. Teleportasi memperlihatkan"
" konversi keadaan qubit stasioner menjadi informasi yang dibawa oleh "
"pasangan yang terjerat (\"flying\") dan komunikasi klasik, yang kemudian "
"digunakan untuk merekonstruksi keadaan pada qubit stasioner lain di tempat "
"lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recommended activity: Take the Qiskit in Classrooms *Quantum Teleportation* "
"module {#recommended-activity-take-the-qiskit-in-classrooms-quantum-"
"teleportation-module}"
msgstr ""
"Aktivitas yang Direkomendasikan: Ikuti modul *Quantum Teleportation* dari "
"Qiskit in Classrooms {#recommended-activity-take-the-qiskit-in-classrooms-"
"quantum-teleportation-module}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit in Classrooms [Quantum "
"Teleportation](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/learning/en/modules/computer-"
"science/quantum-teleportation) module by Dr. Katie McCormick will guide you "
"through one of the most captivating protocols in quantum information: "
"quantum teleportation, where a quantum state (a qubit) is sent from Alice to"
" Bob using entanglement and just two classical bits. You'll learn the full "
"teleportation procedure step-by-step—how to prepare the entangled Bell pair,"
" perform a Bell-basis measurement on Alice’s side, transmit classical "
"results, and apply the correct quantum gate on Bob's qubit to perfectly "
"recover the original state. Along the way, you'll explore why teleporting "
"the information of a qubit doesn't violate the no-cloning theorem or exceed "
"the speed of light. Through hands-on exercises using IBM Quantum hardware or"
" simulators, you'll gain a practical grasp of measurement, entanglement, and"
" feed-forward control in action.\n"
msgstr ""
"Modul [Quantum "
"Teleportation](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/learning/en/modules/computer-"
"science/quantum-teleportation) dari Qiskit in Classrooms oleh Dr. Katie "
"McCormick akan memandu kamu melalui salah satu protokol paling memukau dalam"
" informasi kuantum: teleportasi kuantum, di mana keadaan kuantum (sebuah "
"qubit) dikirim dari Alice ke Bob menggunakan entanglement dan hanya dua bit "
"klasik. Kamu akan mempelajari prosedur teleportasi lengkap langkah demi "
"langkah—cara menyiapkan pasangan Bell yang terjerat, melakukan pengukuran "
"basis Bell di sisi Alice, mengirimkan hasil klasik, dan menerapkan Gate "
"kuantum yang tepat pada qubit Bob untuk memulihkan keadaan asal dengan "
"sempurna. Sepanjang jalan, kamu akan mengeksplorasi mengapa menteleportasi "
"informasi sebuah qubit tidak melanggar teorema no-cloning atau melebihi "
"kecepatan cahaya. Melalui latihan langsung menggunakan hardware IBM Quantum "
"atau simulator, kamu akan mendapatkan pemahaman praktis tentang pengukuran, "
"entanglement, dan kontrol feed-forward dalam aksi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By mastering quantum teleportation, you'll understand how to encode, transmit, and recover quantum information between distinct nodes—laying the foundation for quantum networks, repeater systems, secure communication schemes, and scalable modular quantum computing.\n"
"**How this relates to criteria 6 & 7:** In a real quantum network, the shared entangled pair would be created by distributing \"flying\" qubits (like photons) between Alice and Bob's locations (Criterion 7: faithful transmission). The teleportation protocol itself then serves as a way to map Alice's stationary qubit state onto her half of the entangled pair, effectively 'sending' it to Bob (Criterion 6: interconversion). Qiskit allows us to simulate the protocol's logic perfectly, providing a conceptual model for how these criteria are met in communication architectures.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan menguasai teleportasi kuantum, kamu akan memahami cara mengkode, mengirimkan, dan memulihkan informasi kuantum antara node-node yang berbeda—meletakkan fondasi untuk jaringan kuantum, sistem repeater, skema komunikasi aman, dan komputasi kuantum modular yang dapat diskalakan.\n"
"**Kaitan dengan kriteria 6 & 7:** Dalam jaringan kuantum nyata, pasangan yang terjerat dibuat dengan mendistribusikan \"flying\" Qubit (seperti foton) antara lokasi Alice dan Bob (Kriteria 7: transmisi akurat). Protokol teleportasi itu sendiri kemudian berfungsi sebagai cara untuk memetakan keadaan qubit stasioner Alice ke setengah bagian miliknya dari pasangan yang terjerat, secara efektif 'mengirimkannya' ke Bob (Kriteria 6: interkonversi). Qiskit memungkinkan kita mensimulasikan logika protokol dengan sempurna, memberikan model konseptual tentang bagaimana kriteria-kriteria ini terpenuhi dalam arsitektur komunikasi.\n"

